  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d01fd2d64a9249049aaa77d5c12a82fe, type: 3}
  m_Name: Question 5
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  questionText: '7. The radius of curvature of the plane side of a

    plano-convex
    lens is .......'
  referenceImage: {fileID: 0}
  explanationText: In a plano-convex lens, the radius of curvature of the plane side
    is equal to infinity. As the lens needs to be part of the sphere and for it to
    be flat, the radius of the sphere has to be infinity.
  options:
  - infinity
  - Zero
  - One
  - None of the above
  correctOptionIndex: 0
